@@ -15,3 +15,20 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Passkeys
+
+Readers can sign up, sign in, and reauthenticate with passkeys (WebAuthn, via
+[SimpleWebAuthn](https://simplewebauthn.dev/)), and manage them at `/account`.
+
+- **Sign up** (`/signup`): create a passkey-only account, or sign up with a password and get offered a passkey afterwards.
+- **Sign in** (`/signin`): "Sign in with a passkey" button plus passkey autofill on the username field (conditional UI). After a password sign-in, accounts without a passkey get a silent passkey upgrade where the browser supports it (conditional create), and an explicit prompt otherwise.
+- **Account settings** (`/account`): list, create, rename, and remove passkeys. Adding or removing a passkey requires having signed in or reauthenticated (passkey or password) within the last 5 minutes. The page uses the WebAuthn Signal API to keep passkey providers in sync with the server.
+
+Password checks are still handled by the external Times API, which the server now proxies so it can set a session. Passkeys and passkey-only accounts are stored in a JSON file at `.data/auth.json`.
+
+| Env var | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `PASSKEY_DATA_DIR` | Directory for the passkey store (default `./.data`). Point this at persistent storage in production; Cloud Run's filesystem is temporary. |
+| `WEBAUTHN_RP_ID` | Relying Party ID (default: request hostname). |
+| `WEBAUTHN_ORIGINS` | Comma-separated allowed origins (default: request origin). |
